IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 822 of 2020
CITATION: (2020) 20 SCC 272
YEAR: 2020

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Arun Mishra, Indira Banerjee, M.R. Shah

PARTIES:
Hira Singh vs Union of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 2(viia) NDPS, Section 21 NDPS

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
neutral substance, mixture weight, commercial quantity threshold

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Held that in mixture of narcotic drug and neutral substance, total weight of mixture is to be considered, not just pure drug content, to determine commercial quantity.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 2(viia) NDPS, Section 21 NDPS.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

